# Network/API Rules

- Treat protocol contracts as compatibility-sensitive.
- Validate framing, message size, version, type and payload before dispatch.
- Keep transport concerns separate from domain logic.
- Make connection, timeout, cancellation and reconnect behavior explicit.
- Do not silently accept incompatible protocol versions.
- Public contract changes require documentation and contract tests.
- Never let a remote client directly invoke privileged execution without the runtime safety boundary.
